# Secrets — must never enter an image layer
.env
db/seed.sql
db/seed.local.sql

# Client-confidential
docs/

# VCS and local state
.git/
.gitignore
# **/ is required: a bare __pycache__ matches only the top level, so every
# nested one was being copied in.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Not needed at runtime
tests/
*.md
!README.md

# deploy/ is mostly host-side: shell scripts, the systemd unit, and SQL that is
# piped in from outside the container. None of it belongs in the image.
#
# The Python tools are the exception. They are RUN INSIDE the container, on
# purpose, so they share the same .env, the same database and the same code the
# bot itself is running — a check that used a different client would not be
# checking the thing that matters. Listing the exclusions rather than ignoring
# deploy/ wholesale keeps that explicit, and means the next .py tool added here
# works without anyone remembering this file exists.
deploy/*.sh
deploy/*.sql
deploy/*.service
deploy/*.md

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Backups
*.sql.gz
*.dump
